			"notes": "## What's Changed\n* Upgrade master 1.2.7->1.3.1 by @colinarelliott in https://github.com/colinarelliott/Utility-Golems/pull/44\n* Merge from 1.3.1->1.3.5 by @colinarelliott in https://github.com/colinarelliott/Utility-Golems/pull/49\n* Merge version 1.4.7 of dev into master by @colinarelliott in https://github.com/colinarelliott/Utility-Golems/pull/62\n\n## Bug Fixes\n- Bamboo golems farm nicely again\n- Amethyst golems don't get stuck withdrawing extra seeds\n- UI fixes across the board and some server to client sync issues from the new versions of Minecraft.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/colinarelliott/Utility-Golems/compare/1.4.6...1.4.7\n\n### Fixed\n- **Networking was broken for every serverbound packet.** Reflecting on Fabric's\n  non-public context class threw `IllegalAccessException`, silently killing the Jukebox\n  controls, Emerald trade selection, Redstone Start/Reset, Diamond build-pattern sync\n  and Cactus slot clearing. Resolved through the public API interface instead.\n- **Jukebox Golem UI rebuilt.** The playlist holds 9 discs again (was 1), Play/Stop,\n  Shuffle and Repeat work and show their state, and the window is drawn correctly.\n  Slots only accept music discs, and a \"Playing:\" line names the current track.\n- **Jukebox playback.** Tracks ran at double speed (cooldown ticked twice), every disc\n  played twice over itself, finished discs were duplicated onto the ground, and ending a\n  track silenced *all* nearby jukeboxes. Pressing Play after a playlist finished did\n  nothing. The playlist is now also dropped when the golem dies.\n- **Amethyst Golems no longer pester their chest** when already stocked with breeding\n  food ([#60](https://github.com/colinarelliott/Utility-Golems/issues/60)).\n- **Farm Golems now harvest the whole field** ([#61](https://github.com/colinarelliott/Utility-Golems/issues/61)).\n  They tilled and planted within 16 blocks of the water source but only harvested within\n  `workRadius` (default 8) of the chest, so the outer field was planted and never reaped.\n  Both now use the same area. Also fixes the stripped pumpkin/melon mode.\n- Golem screens were dimming the background and drawing their titles twice.\n\n### Changed\n- **Redstone Golem UI polished** and marked **W.I.P** — it now has a proper background,\n  a layout where the controls no longer overlap the inventory slots, centred slot grids,\n  and readable block names in the program list. Functionality is still in flux.\n- Farm Golems cache their field scan per tick and no longer reserve a work target while\n  other goals are merely checking whether farm work exists."
		},
